      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakersfield%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Joseph Baker built grist and saw mills on Baker's Pond in 1794 to support the early settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakersfield%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bakersfield is part of the Missisquoi River watershed, which eventually drains into Lake Champlain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakersfield%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Cold Hollow Mountains occupy the eastern end of Bakersfield, reaching a high point of over three thousand feet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
